    7. raw_kernel_scalar

[5] Readout
  The kernel-homotopy rule is a proof-interface guardrail, not a proof of
  LRC14.  Open components are stable under small kernel support changes and
  can feed HYP-2981-style Fejer interval certificates.  AP/GW have no such
  support radius; they are boundary-defect atoms and must remain labelled.
  A future smoothing proof must therefore state exactly which labels survive
  the homotopy and which boundary defects are emitted.
